The green check marks Current: the available package matches Latest release. The brown clock marks Outdated: an older or different available version. Completed publication appears as `—` in In build because no replacement remains in progress. Pending waits for a build; Superseded was replaced by a newer release or attempt; Not built has no recorded build. Filled indicators mean a package exists or work is happening; rings mean nothing yet or stopped. The filled Failed cross records a failed attempt, not package availability. Alternative text and hover titles name every state. `—` means no available package, no replacement in progress, or an unrecorded fact, according to the column. Build log identifies the verified source job; no link is shown until one exists.
